-- title:
--   Centre of V is a minimal prime over varpi in the finite chart
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative domain which is a discrete valuation ring, let $\varpi \in R$ be such that the maximal ideal of $R$ equals the ideal generated by $\varpi$, let $F$ be a field equipped with an $R$-algebra structure and let $j \in F$ be non-zero. Write $A =$ `chartAlgFin R F j` for the $R$-subalgebra of $F$ consisting of those $x \in F$ that are integral over the $R$-subalgebra $R[j] =$ `Algebra.adjoin R {j}` of $F$. Let $V$ be a valuation subring of $F$ such that: the image of every element of $R$ in $F$ lies in $V$; the image of every element of the maximal ideal of $R$ lies in the set of non-units of $V$; and for every polynomial $P \in R[X]$ whose reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $R$ is non-zero, both $P(j)$ and $P(j)^{-1}$ lie in $V$. The conclusion asserts the existence of an ideal $\mathfrak{P}$ of $A$ which is prime, satisfies $b \in \mathfrak{P} \iff b \in \mathrm{nonunits}(V)$ for every $b \in A$ (viewing $b$ in $F$), contains the image of $\varpi$ in $A$, and is a minimal prime over the ideal of $A$ generated by that image of $\varpi$.
--
--   This identifies the centre of $V$ in the finite chart of the two-chart integral model as a minimal prime of the special fibre, so that the point of $\operatorname{Spec} A$ cut out by $V$ lies on the special fibre with no intervening prime. It is used in the analysis of the full-level modular curve, where it is invoked for supersingular $j$-invariants to show that an element whose image lies in the non-units of such a valuation subring belongs to a prescribed maximal ideal.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel_exists_isPrime_mem_iff_mem_nonunits_mem_minimalPrimes_span_of_valuationSubring.lean

